    "description": "•\tSuccessfully developed an embedded Qt/QML based control device with superior quality, on time, and within budget.   Developed end-to-end features, which involved highly customized user interface.  Since first customer shipment for over 8 months there has been 0 customer found defects.  Granted numerous awards for a job well done\n•\tDeveloping next generation android-based Cisco touch control device for Cisco TelePresence.  Followed agile and lean development practices to improve speed and quality of product.  In just 4 months a small team and I were able to go from 0 android knowledge to delivering an android control device which was feature parity with first generation device.   To keep software quality at its highest we utilized unit and integration testing tools such as Robotium, Roboelectric, and JUint\n•\tWorked very closely with User Experience group and Project Management to help deliver a solid product.  I’m a very positive and friendly person who enjoys interacting and problem solving in a team environment\n•\tExperience in writing design, functional, and test documents for feature development.  Developed a lean process to help speed up product release to testing team and another document to help ensure software quality by following DPAI process  \n•\tIn charge of leading a key set of software features to dev test.  Successfully created a schedule with tight deadlines, delivery plan, and supported the team in reaching their goals\n•\tDrove scrum meetings as scrum master to help improve quality and faster delivery of software.\n•\tChampioned mentoring an intern, provided technical advice and people skill coaching.  Successfully drove intern to develop a cool feature of a whiteboard application based on HTML5\n•\tInvolved in patent brain storming sessions, which helped generate new ideas for video collaboration",
